---

<section id="hero" class="bg-gradient-to-br from-blue-50 via-white to-blue-100 border-base-200 overflow-hidden" style="background: linear-gradient(to bottom right, #D4E7F4, white, #D4E7F4);">
  <div class="px-8 pt-14 md:pt-28 lg:pt-40 mx-auto md:px-12 lg:px-24 max-w-7xl relative pb-20">
    <div class="max-w-3xl text-center mx-auto lg:text-balance mb-10">
      
      <!-- Platform Badge -->
      <div class="mb-6">
        <span class="inline-block px-4 py-2 rounded-full text-sm font-semibold" style="background-color: #3a5a8c; color: white;">
          Mobile App Only • iOS App Store
        </span>
      </div>

      <h1 class="text-3xl leading-tight tracking-tight sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl mt-4 font-bold" style="color: var(--color-text-primary)">
        Trauma Recovery Resource and Support Tool
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg md:text-xl leading-relaxed mt-6 font-medium" style="color: var(--color-text-secondary)">
        Compassionate, trauma-informed emotional support available 24/7. Process triggers, track healing, and regulate your nervous system—all in one mobile app.
      </p>
      
      <!-- CTA Button -->
      <div class="flex items-center justify-center mt-10">
        <a href="#" class="inline-block">
          <img 
            src="https://tools.applemediaservices.com/api/badges/download-on-the-app-store/black/en-us?size=250x83&releaseDate=1276560000" 
            alt="Download on the App Store" 
            class="h-14 w-auto"
          />
        </a>
      </div>

      <!-- Trial Info -->
      <p class="text-sm mt-4" style="color: var(--color-text-secondary)">
        7-day free trial • $11.99/month after • Cancel anytime
      </p>

      <!-- Crisis Disclaimer -->
      <div class="mt-8 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        <div class="bg-blue-50 border-l-4 border-blue-400 p-4 rounded-lg">
          <p class="text-sm text-black !text-black leading-relaxed">
            <strong>Trauma Recovery Resource:</strong> ProcessIt is a trauma-informed recovery resource, not medical treatment or therapy. This tool is designed to complement professional mental health care, not replace it. If you're experiencing a crisis, please contact emergency services (911) or the 988 Suicide & Crisis Lifeline.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>